{
  "$comment": [
    "PRD_FOOD 8.2's usual portions. Ciqual publishes none: it is a composition table, and",
    "'how much of this does a person eat at once' is not composition. So this file is a",
    "product decision written by hand, and it is deliberately short.",
    "",
    "The asymmetry that governs it: a wrong calorie figure is visible, because 400 kcal",
    "for a tomato looks wrong to anyone. A wrong portion weight is invisible - '1 bowl'",
    "at 250 g when the user's bowl holds 400 g produces a number that looks entirely",
    "reasonable and is 60 % out, every time, silently. PRD_FOOD 8.6 also says the portion",
    "is only ever an aid to entry and that an exact weight always takes precedence, which",
    "is the escape hatch, not a licence to guess.",
    "",
    "So a portion is written only where the food comes in a unit a person actually",
    "handles: an egg, a yoghurt pot, a slice of bread, an apple, a glass. There is",
    "deliberately no portion for rice, pasta, minced meat, cheese by weight, flour or",
    "sugar by the spoon - foods someone either weighs or estimates, and neither is helped",
    "by a number Mue invented.",
    "",
    "Every weight is validated against PRD_FOOD 15's 1..2 000 g at build time and a bad",
    "one fails the build. `code` is the Ciqual alim_code, and every one below was checked",
    "against the release in ciqual.source.json and against the emitted subset; a portion",
    "written for a food the subset does not ship is printed in the build report."
  ],
